.TH SDL_iconv_string 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_iconv_string \- Helper function to convert a string\(aqs encoding in one call.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "char * SDL_iconv_string(const char *tocode,
.BI "                   const char *fromcode,
.BI "                   const char *inbuf,
.BI "                   size_t inbytesleft);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function converts a buffer or string between encodings in one pass\[char46]
.PP
The string does not need to be NULL-terminated; this function operates on the number of bytes specified in
.BR inbytesleft
whether there is a NULL character anywhere in the buffer\[char46]
.PP
The returned string is owned by the caller, and should be passed to
.BR SDL_free
when no longer needed\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I tocode
the character encoding of the output string\[char46] Examples are \(dqUTF-8\(dq, \(dqUCS-4\(dq, etc\[char46]
.TP
.I fromcode
the character encoding of data in
.BR inbuf \[char46]

.TP
.I inbuf
the string to convert to a different encoding\[char46]
.TP
.I inbytesleft
the size of the input string _in bytes_\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a new string, converted to the new encoding, or NULL on error\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_iconv_open (3),
.BR SDL_iconv_close (3),
.BR SDL_iconv (3)
